From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0800: scaled_copy_levers 16: swap_direct_present at a draw resolution scale above 1 reproduces the front buffer resolve's half-pixel fill, so the picture is exact (Direct3D 12; native stream, direct present at 2000p)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; design note scratch/dp2x/DESIGN.md). Written without a build or a run: checked with
  clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags, no PCH) of the 4 changed translation units and 13 that include the changed
  headers: 0 errors, no new warning. The 3 DXBC headers are built with fxc 10.0.26100.0 (scratch/dp2x/make_dp2x_shaders.py); the
  toolchain reproduced the shipped bytecode of the 3 shaders they are copies of (apply_gamma_table_cs, apply_gamma_table_fxaa_luma_cs,
  guest_output_gamma_table_ps) bit for bit before they were built, and the disassembly of each new one differs from its original only by the
  clamp (umax / imax of the pixel index with the fill constant).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause); the 3 shaders are Xenia
  (BSD) code with the clamp added
Purpose: Make swap_direct_present (04a0) exact at a draw resolution scale of 2 (profile 2000p), where 0760 could only offer it with a stripe.
  Cause (read from the code, and from runs r1-sw2 / r1-px / r1-px9 / r1-fin): the guest draws its full-screen passes with the half-pixel
  offset, which at scale 2 moves the quad by one host pixel (04e0's log: the surely covered rectangle is 1,1 1599x999), so host row 0 and host
  column 0 of the render target are never written by the frame. The front buffer's resolve at scale > 1 (resolve_resolution_scale_fill_half_pixel_offset,
  default true; draw.cpp ResolveInfo color_edram_info.fill_half_pixel_offset; resolve.xesli half_pixel_offset_fill_source = resolution_scale >> 1;
  resolve_direct_{full,fast}_{32,64}bpp.xesli) writes the area's pixel (x, y) as the render target's (max(x, fill), max(y, fill)), fill = scale >> 1 per axis, so
  the loaded texture the swap reads has row 0 / column 0 filled from the next ones. The direct present reads the render target itself and showed its
  stale row 0 and column 0: in swap_direct_present_check 100 of 111 checks differ, 90 of them in all 5,199 = 3200 + 2000 - 1 pixels of the first row and
  column (up to 1023 in 10 bits) and 10 in 4,999 to 5,065 (some of the pixels agree by chance), and all 111 have 0 differences anywhere else; the 11 exact
  ones are the first 11 checks, the boot and loading frames (black or flat, where the fill changes nothing: the screenshots of r1-px at 4, 8 and 12 s are
  all black), and from the first 3D frame (16 s) row 0 differs from row 1 in 3,200 of 3,200 pixels of the screenshot (the controls r1-fin and r1-px9, levers 9, in 0 to 153).
  Fix: scaled_copy_levers bit 16 (range now 0..31; with 2; default 0 = unchanged): the passes that read the render target in place read it at
  max(pixel, fill): the apply-gamma compute passes (new apply_gamma_table_fill_cs and apply_gamma_table_fxaa_luma_fill_cs, the push constants
  grow from the size to the size and the fill; the FXAA one is the ultra preset's path), the presenter's fused gamma paint (new
  guest_output_gamma_table_fill_ps; its root constants grow from 2 to 4 values), and swap_direct_present_check's passes. The record of the front
  buffer's resolve keeps whether it filled (0760's field); bit 16 accepts a filled record like bit 4 and makes the reads fill, bit 4 alone stays the
  old stripe (do not use it). HDR output reads the loaded texture for such a picture (the hdr_refresh shaders are not changed); frame generation
  already does. No effect at a scale of 1 or with the lever off; the old pipelines and shaders run as before wherever the fill is 0.
Bucket: REDO

0800-swap-direct-present-scaled-fill.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, direct present at 2000p). Applies after 0780 (the last entry of the series).

